WEBVTT

00:03:27.802 --> 00:03:31.073
in a certain way which has nothing to do with casual speech.

00:03:31.073 --> 00:03:34.932
It's formal. It uses long sentences like this Gibbon one.

00:03:34.932 --> 00:03:38.894
It's basically talking like you write, and so, for example,

00:03:38.894 --> 00:03:40.889
we're thinking so much these days about Lincoln

00:03:40.889 --> 00:03:43.100
because of the movie.

00:03:43.100 --> 00:03:46.183
The Gettysburg Address was not the main meal of that event.

00:03:46.183 --> 00:03:50.098
For two hours before that, Edward Everett spoke

00:03:50.098 --> 00:03:53.338
on a topic that, frankly, cannot engage us today

00:03:53.338 --> 00:03:54.835
and barely did then.

00:03:54.835 --> 00:03:57.216
The point of it was to listen to him

00:03:57.216 --> 00:03:58.772
speaking like writing.

00:03:58.772 --> 00:04:01.120
Ordinary people stood and listened to that for two hours.